What is Playwright and why is it better than Selenium in some cases?
Playwright is a modern automation testing framework developed by Microsoft used for:

Web UI automation
API testing
Cross-browser testing
End-to-end testing

It supports:

Chromium
Firefox
WebKit

and languages like:

Java
JavaScript
TypeScript
Python
C#
“Playwright is a modern open-source automation 
framework developed by Microsoft for end-to-end web testing. It supports multiple browsers and provides fast, 
reliable, and stable automation with features like auto-waiting, parallel execution, network interception, multiple browser contexts, 
and built-in API testing.

Compared to Selenium, Playwright is better in some cases because it reduces flaky tests, handles modern web applications more effectively, and provides faster execution with less setup.
